  "problem": "What are the dimensions of $CD$, if $C$ is a $5\\times 7$ matrix and $D$ is a $7\\times 1$ matrix?",
  "worked_solution": "There are $7$ columns in $C$ and $7$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $C$ equals the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication, and $CD$ is a $5\\times 1$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{C}_{5\\times \\boxed{\\text{7}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{D}_{\\boxed{\\text{7}}\\times 1}={CD}_{5\\times 1}\n$$",
